<title>GHANA: Ghana's Mobil year profits rise sharply.</title>
<headline>Ghana's Mobil year profits rise sharply.</headline>
<dateline>ACCRA 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year profits of Ghana's Mobil petroleum products marketing company to the end of December 1996. (In billion cedis unless stated).</p>
<p>				 1996		  1995</p>
<p>Operating profit	   19.04		 8.90</p>
<p>Profit after tax	   13.40		 4.90</p>
<p>				-----------------------</p>
<p>NOTE: A half year dividend of 616 cedis per share was approved by directors.</p>
<p>General Manager Michael George Riding said sales volume had increased by five percent and this coupled with price rises was responsible for an increase in annual turnover of 37 percent.</p>
<p>He said profits were boosted by the sale of some of the company's property in Ghana.</p>
<p>($1=2000 cedis)</p>
<p>-- Abidjan newsroom +225 21 90 90</p>
